  "worked_solution": "The integers consist of all positive and negative whole numbers and zero.\n\n$$\n…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…\n$$\n\n \n\nOf the given numbers, $100$ and $-5$ are integers, but $-\\frac{9}{2}$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
